02013;32. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16262964</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR24"><label>24.</label><citation citation-type="book"><source>An analysis of the literature on disease managmeent programs</source><year>2004</year><publisher-loc>Washington, DC</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Congress of the United States</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Congressional Budget Office. An analysis of the literature on disease managmeent programs. Washington, DC: Congress of the United States; 2004. </citation></ref><ref id="CR25"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nash</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An open letter to the disease management community</article-title><source>Dis Manag</source><year>2004</year><volume>7</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>266</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/dis.2004.7.265</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Nash DB. An open letter to the disease management community. Dis Manag. 2004;7(4):265&#x02013;6. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15671783</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR26"><label>26.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weingarten</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Henning</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Badamgarav</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Interventions used in disease management programmes for patients with chronic illness&#x02014;which ones work? Meta-analysis of published reports</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2002</year><volume>325</volume><issue>7370</issue><fpage>925</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.325.7370.925</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Weingarten SR, Henning JM, Badamgarav E, et al. Interventions used in disease management programmes for patients with chronic illness&#x02014;which ones work? Meta-analysis of published reports. BMJ. 2002;325(7370):925. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12399340</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR27"><label>27.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ofman</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Badamgarav</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Henning</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Does disease management improve clinical and economic outcomes in patients with chronic diseases? A systematic review</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>117</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>182</fpage><lpage>192</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.amjmed.2004.03.018</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Ofman JJ, Badamgarav E, Henning JM, et al. Does disease management improve clinical and economic outcomes in patients with chronic diseases? A systematic review. Am J Med. 2004;117(3):182&#x02013;92. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15300966</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR28"><label>28.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goetzel</surname><given-names>RZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozminowski</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Villagra</surname><given-names>VG</given-names></name><name><surname>Duffy</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Return on Investment in Disease Management: A Review</article-title><source>Health Care Financ Rev</source><year>2005</year><volume>26</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>19</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Goetzel RZ, Ozminowski RJ, Villagra VG, Duffy J. Return on Investment in Disease Management: A Review. Health Care Financ Rev. 2005;26(4):1&#x02